'''Clanless''' [[file:ClanClanless.png|20x20px]] cards are [[Cards]] that do not belong to any specific clan, and can therefore be acquired on any given run. In the case of [[Spells]] and [[Units]], these cards are typically acquired from [[Celestial Alcove|Celestial Alcoves]], while [[Equipment]] and [[Rooms]] can be obtained from drafts and the [[Merchants#Merchant_of_Arms|Merchant of Arms]] as normal.

All [[Blights]] and [[Scourges]] are considered clanless.

{{ClanlessNav}}

Equipment:
'''Equipment''' is a card type in Monster Train 2. Equipment cards are attached to units on the train. Once attached, they provide the unit with new abilities, effects, and sometimes {{Attack}} and/or {{Health}}. Equipment can only be played on friendly units, with the exceptions of [[Penitent's Bloodsuit]] and [[Penitent's Deathsuit]].

Only one equipment can be attached to a unit at a time. When an equipment card is played on a unit that already has equipment, the old equipment is replaced and its benefits are lost.

In the [[Lazarus League]] clan, [[Graft]] units have equipment pre-attached. These equipment are added to your hand when the units die.

== Obtaining ==
Clan-specific equipment can be obtained from standard card drafts. The {{IconLink|Merchant of Arms|bold=f|png=MerchantOfArms}} sells both clan-specific and Clanless equipment.

The Merchant of Arms also offers two services that can enhance your equipment. One allows you to create [[Merged Equipment]], combining the effects and {{Ember}} costs of two equipment into a single card. The other allows you to apply '''[[Deployable]]''' to an equipment card. Both services cost {{Gold|75}}.

== Triggers ==

The {{IconLink|Equipped|bold=f}} trigger activates when an Equipment card is played on a unit. The {{IconLink|Artificer|bold=f}} trigger activates when an Equipment card is played on any unit on the floor. Both triggers activate immediately when a Graft unit is played.

